{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "07", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "07", "M": "50", "S": "28"}}, "news": [{"title": "Keralam sets two year deadline for setting up logistics parks", "para": "Keralam has rolled out a new framework for logistics parks, requiring developers to show substantial progress within a two-year timeline. These guidelines apply equally to private projects and public-private partnerships, ensuring each initiative is backed by a strong implementation strategy. A single-window clearance board will facilitate quicker approvals, while investment subsidies will be available based on project milestones, provided the chosen areas avoid ecologically sensitive zones or existing parks.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/keralam-sets-two-year-deadline-for-setting-up-logistics-parks/134755777?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-244284/134755777.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "allied-industries"}, {"title": "Gurugram civic body approves construction debris collection up to 500 tonnes daily", "para": "Gurugram's Municipal Corporation has taken a positive step by approving a budget specifically for enhancing door-to-door construction waste collection and sanitation services. Key projects sanctioned by the Finance and Contract Committee include increasing workforce and machinery dedicated to sanitation. With a focus on improving waste management systems, the corporation aims to minimize debris in public areas, demonstrating its commitment to robust sanitation services throughout all municipal zones.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/gurugram-civic-body-approves-construction-debris-collection-up-to-500-tonnes-daily/134755749?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-202058/134755749.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "House tax defaulters in Varanasi warned of assets attachment after November 15", "para": "The Varanasi Municipal Corporation has delivered a final ultimatum to building owners regarding overdue house taxes. A special one-time settlement initiative allows defaulters to evade surcharges by signing up before November 15. Despite being available for over a month and a half, few have taken advantage of this offer.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/house-tax-defaulters-in-varanasi-warned-of-assets-attachment-after-november-15/134755707?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-59138/134755707.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}